{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>YHWH will establish you for Himself as a holy people, as He swore to you</b> — He calls the covenant that He made with them at Mount Sinai concerning all these things an \"oath,\" for there it is stated (Exodus 19:6), \"And you shall be to Me a kingdom of priests and a holy nation.\" Or, the covenant that He made with Abraham (Genesis 17:7), \"to be to you for an Elohim and for your seed after you,\" includes this. And so He said (Deuteronomy 29:12), \"in order to establish you today for Himself as a people, and He will be to you for an Elohim, as He spoke to you and as He swore to your fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob\" — for all of them enter into the covenant:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:56:19.144648966Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}